    #  R2. The target is a directory under the worktree that does not exist yet.
    #  R3. The target is a symbolic link outside the worktree pointing into it.
    #  R4. An unknown tier: "e", and "A" (the tiers are lower case).
    #  R5. The wrong argument count: none, one, and three (an extra argument
    #      other than --force).
    #  R6. Tier t generated into a fresh target outside the worktree (the
    #      positive control: exit 0, one generated line of the documented
    #      form, one manifest row, one workbook), then the same call again
    #      without --force: refused, the manifest and the workbook unchanged.
    #  R7. The same call with --force: exit 0, the manifest still holds exactly
    #      one row whose tags column is scale,tiert, with the same id (the
    #      generator is deterministic), and one workbook in the corpus.
    #  R8. A leftover partial file .tier-t.xlsx.part in a fresh target, no
    #      --force: refused, the partial file unchanged, no manifest, no
    #      workbook.
    #  R9. A manifest with another header in a fresh target: refused, the
    #      manifest unchanged, no workbook.
    #  R10. The workbook's file already in a fresh target's corpus with no
    #      manifest row (the existing file of another target copied there), no
    #      --force: refused after the generation, the file unchanged, no partial
    #      file left, no manifest.
    #  R11. A copy of the generator beside a copy of the crate's template whose
    #      worksheet has lost its <sheetData/> anchor: refused with the anchor
    #      message, no partial file, no manifest.
